.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt AUGITE-SETUP 1
.Os Augite 0.1.0
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm augite-setup
.Nd set or show repository metadata
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "augite setup"
.Oo
.Fl d
.Ar text No \&|
.Fl "-description"
.Ar text
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl o
.Ar name No \&|
.Fl "-owner"
.Ar name
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl u
.Ar url No \&|
.Fl "-url"
.Ar url
.Oc
.Ar repo-dir
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "augite setup"
writes the description,
owner and clone URL that Augite displays for the repository
at
.Ar repo-dir .
Only the fields specified on the command line are changed.
An empty value removes the corresponding file.
.Pp
Without options,
the command prints the current description,
owner and clone URL.
Missing values are shown as empty fields.
.Pp
Metadata is stored in files named
.Ql "description" ,
.Ql "owner"
and
.Ql "url" .
The command writes them in the repository’s
.Eo
.Pa .git/
.Ec
directory when it is a directory,
or in
.Ar repo-dir
itself for a bare repository.
When reading metadata,
Augite first looks in
.Ar repo-dir
and then in its
.Eo
.Pa .git/
.Ec
directory,
as in stagit.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl d ,
.Fl "-description"
.Ar text
.Xc
Sets the one-line description.
An empty value removes it.
.It Xo
.Fl o ,
.Fl "-owner"
.Ar name
.Xc
Sets the owner.
An empty value removes it.
.It Xo
.Fl u ,
.Fl "-url"
.Ar url
.Xc
Sets the URL to clone from.
An empty value removes it.
This is separate from the site’s base URL accepted by
.Xr augite-repo 1 .
.It Xo
.Fl h ,
.Fl "-help"
.Xc
Prints a usage summary and exits.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Set metadata for a bare repository on the server:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ augite setup -d \(dqThe Analytical Engine\(dq --owner \(dqAda Lovelace\(dq \e
    -u https://example\&.org/engine\&.git /var/git/engine\&.git
.Ed
.Pp
Show the current values,
then remove the owner:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ augite setup /var/git/engine\&.git
$ augite setup --owner \(dq\(dq /var/git/engine\&.git
.Ed
.Pp
Set the description in the current repository’s
.Eo
.Pa .git/
.Ec
directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ augite setup -d \(dqThe Analytical Engine\(dq \&.
.Ed
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr augite 1 ,
.Xr augite-index 1 ,
.Xr augite-repo 1
.
